Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21411) Support selective redelivery of
 records in share groups
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Shekhar Prasad Rajak (Jira) via dev" <dev@kafka.apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>
Cc: "Shekhar Prasad Rajak (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>

Shekhar Prasad Rajak created KAFKA-21411:
--------------------------------------------

             Summary: Support selective redelivery of records in share grou=
ps
                 Key: KAFKA-21411
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21411
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Shekhar Prasad Rajak


Introduce an operation that makes explicitly selected retained records AVAI=
LABLE again in the same share group, while preserving delivery eligibility =
and retained processing metadata outside the selection.

Applications may need to reprocess selected inputs after correcting a trans=
formation, repairing an application defect, or recovering a durable process=
ing manifest. Current RELEASE acknowledgements apply to acquired records, w=
hile partition offset reset does not preserve an arbitrary sparse selection=
 of completed records.

For example:

Previously completed:
Worker A: 100=E2=80=93104, 150=E2=80=93154
Worker B: 105=E2=80=93149

Requested selection:
100=E2=80=93104, 150=E2=80=93154

Expected result:
A=E2=80=99s selected records become AVAILABLE again.
B=E2=80=99s completed records remain excluded from delivery.

---

KIP https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/x/5AKWGw=20



