Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

Hi Nicole,

Thanks for the KIP! The KIP looks good, just a few minor comments:

RS01: Can we add a link to the KIP in the KIPs under discussion table in
https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/spaces/KAFKA/pages/50859233/Kafka+Impro=
vement+Proposals
?

RS02: The KIP gives an example of using `all()` instead of `valid()`. Since
we talk about MirrorMaker in the motivation section, it will be good to
include details about how MirrorMaker can be updated to use this KIP. In
addition to calling ListGroupsOptions.forConsumerGroups().
requireCommittedOffsets(true)).all().get();  , MM2 would also need to retry
without requireCommittedOffsets on  UnsupportedVersionException?

RS03: The KIP says that the filter "*adds a per-group in-memory existence
check*". Is this just a boolean check or does it need anything additional
for the semantics described in the KIP?

Thanks,

Rajini

On Wed, Oct 28, 2026 at 4:28=E2=80=AFPM Nicole Du <nicoleywdu@gmail.com> wr=
ote:

> Hi David,
>
> Thanks for taking a look and for the suggestions!
>
> For DJ01: My reasoning was to keep the predicate focused on offsets that
> have already been committed. Pending transactional offsets may still be
> aborted, so they do not count on their own. A group with an existing
> committed offset still matches even if it also has pending offsets.
>
> I=E2=80=99ve clarified this in the KIP. One trade-off is that a pending-o=
nly group
> that commits after the listing is evaluated needs a subsequent listing to
> be discovered. I=E2=80=99d appreciate your thoughts on whether including
> pending-only groups would be more useful for callers.
>
> For DJ02: That makes sense. I=E2=80=99ve replaced the snapshot-specific w=
ording
> with a definition based on the coordinator=E2=80=99s committed state and =
simplified
> the table to three cases: at least one committed offset, pending offsets
> only, and neither. A separate sentence clarifies that offsets eligible fo=
r
> expiration continue to count until their deletion takes effect.
>
> I=E2=80=99ve also made two small updates to the existing test plan: expli=
citly
> covering pending offsets through transaction commit and abort, and
> describing the visibility test in terms of committed state.
>
> Best,
> Nicole
>
> On Wed, Oct 28, 2026 at 7:51=E2=80=AFAM David Jacot <dajac@apache.org> wr=
ote:
>
> > Hi Nicole,
> >
> > Thanks for the KIP! I have only two comments:
> >
> > DJ01: What's the reasoning for not including groups with only pending
> > offsets?
> > DJ02: I wonder if we should simplify the "State of the group at the
> > read snapshot" table. For instance, "is visible in the snapshot" is an
> > implementation detail. We should rather say that the condition is
> > applied to the committed state and simplify the table.
> >
> > Best,
> > David
> >
> >
> > On Mon, Oct 26, 2026 at 11:49=E2=80=AFPM Nicole Du <nicoleywdu@gmail.co=
m> wrote:
> > >
> > > Hi all,
> > >
> > > I'd like to start a discussion on KIP-1388, which proposes adding a
> > > request-side filter to the ListGroups API to allow Admin.listGroups t=
o
> > > return only groups with at least one committed offset.
> > >
> > > Tools that replicate consumer group offsets across clusters, such as
> > > MirrorMaker 2 and the group offset sync in KIP-1279, typically list a=
ll
> > > groups before fetching their offsets. In large deployments, many grou=
ps
> > may
> > > have active members but no committed offsets, resulting in unnecessar=
y
> > > OffsetFetch requests and additional load on group coordinators.
> > >
> > > This KIP proposes filtering these groups on the server side by
> > introducing
> > > a new request field in ListGroups v6 and exposing it through
> > > ListGroupsOptions.requireCommittedOffsets(boolean).
> > >
> > > KIP:
> > >
> >
> https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1388%3A+Add+a+commi=
tted-offsets+filter+to+ListGroups
> > >
> > > JIRA: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21366
> > >
> > > I'd appreciate any feedback or suggestions.
> > >
> > > Thanks,
> > > Nicole
> >
>

