> Hi Ming-Yen
>
> chia_00:
> Why does the new handler need to throw an exception when it sees the
> unsecuredLogin* configs? Those belong to another handler, so I don=E2=80=
=99t get
> the point of checking them here.
>
> chia_01:
> Should OAuthBearerUnsecuredLoginCallbackHandler switch to use warn level
> instead of info level?
> ```java
> log.info("Token not provided since n ...
> ```
>
> Best,
> Chia-Ping
>
> On 2026-11-02 02:21 UTC Ming-Yen Chung wrote:
> > Hi all,
> >
> > I would like to start a discussion on
> > KIP-1390: Add a tokenless login callback handler for SASL/OAUTHBEARER
> > <https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/x/qAKWGw>
> >
> > A broker that only validates OAuth tokens does not need its own token,
> but
> > today it relies on the internal OAuthBearerUnsecuredLoginCallbackHandle=
r
> to
> > log in without one. This KIP proposes a new
> > OAuthBearerTokenlessLoginCallbackHandler to support tokenless login
> > officially.
> >
> > Best,
> > Ming-Yen
> >
>

