Subject: Re: [DISCUSS] Apache Kafka 3.9.3 release
To: dev@kafka.apache.org
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
From: Mickael Maison <mickael.maison@gmail.com>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Hi,

I'm not opposing making another 3.9 bugfix release but I think we
should clarify our position regarding 3.9.
3.9.0 was released 2 years ago and it's not marked as supported anymore.

I understand there's been a lot of CVEs published recently. However
considering the current trends it's likely there will be more, so will
we consider making a 3.9.4 release?
The reason I'm raising this is to set clear expectations for our
users, and to balance our workload as maintaining extra releases has a
cost.

Thanks,
Mickael



