Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21419) KRaft controller drops still-adding
 replicas from addingReplicas when an in-progress reassignment is overridden
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Haifeng Chen (Jira) via dev" <dev@kafka.apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>
Cc: "Haifeng Chen (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>

Haifeng Chen created KAFKA-21419:
------------------------------------

             Summary: KRaft controller drops still-adding replicas from add=
ingReplicas when an in-progress reassignment is overridden
                 Key: KAFKA-21419
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21419
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: controller
    Affects Versions: 4.3.0, 4.2.0, 4.1.0, 4.0.0
            Reporter: Haifeng Chen


When a partition reassignment is still in progress and a new reassignment f=
or the same partition is submitted (for example with {{{}kafka-reassign-par=
titions.sh --execute --additional{}}}, which Cruise Control does routinely)=
, the KRaft controller computes the new {{addingReplicas}} as {{{}target =
=E2=88=92 currentReplicas{}}}. {{currentReplicas}} already contains the rep=
licas the first reassignment is still adding, so any of them that are also =
in the new target are silently promoted to plain replicas even though they =
have not joined the ISR yet.

The override then completes as soon as the replicas it newly adds are in sy=
nc, leaving the partition with a replica that is out of the ISR and that no=
 reassignment accounts for: {{--list}} shows nothing in flight, {{--verify}=
} reports success, under-replicated partitions stay non-zero until the repl=
ica happens to catch up, and the removing replica is dropped while the part=
ition has fewer in-sync replicas than it looks.

Reproduction (any KRaft cluster):
 # Partition on {{{}[1,2,3]{}}}; reassign to {{[1,2,4]}} and hold broker 4 =
out of the ISR (e.g. 1 B/s follower throttle). {{--list}} shows {{adding: 4=
. removing: 3.}}

 # While 4 is still adding, run {{--execute --additional}} with {{{}[1,2,4,=
5]{}}}.

 # {{--list}} shows {{adding: 5. removing: 3.}} =E2=80=94 4 is gone from ad=
ding.

 # Once 5 is in sync the reassignment completes: {{{}replicas=3D[1,2,4,5] i=
sr=3D[1,2,5]{}}}, no reassignment in progress.

Expected: step 3 shows {{adding: 4,5. removing: 3.}} and the reassignment s=
tays in progress until 4 is also in sync.

The override case is only correct today when the new adding set happens to =
be empty (the builder leaves the old one in place) or when the RF-reduction=
 guard {{adding.size() < removing.size()}} blocks completion, which masks t=
he bug for shrinking overrides.

ZooKeeper-mode controllers computed the new adding set relative to the orig=
inal replica set, so this is a KRaft regression.

Fix: derive the new adding set as {{{}target =E2=88=92 (currentReplicas =E2=
=88=92 currentAddingReplicas){}}}, so a replica that was still being added =
by the previous reassignment stays in {{addingReplicas}} if the new target =
keeps it.



