Hi Rajini,

Thanks for the questions!

For RS01: Done.

For RS02: Yes, MM2 would need to retry without the option to support older
brokers. It currently uses valid(), so it could preserve its existing
handling of partial results by inspecting errors() on the same
ListGroupsResult. If any error is an UnsupportedVersionException, it would
retry once with only requireCommittedOffsets disabled, keeping the other
filters unchanged. The retry result would replace the initial result. I
have added this adoption guidance to the KIP and clarified that changes to
MM2 itself are not proposed here.

For RS03: An existence lookup is sufficient. The committed-offsets map
removes a group's entry when its last offset is deleted, and offsets of
uncommitted transactions are stored separately. Checking for the group's
entry against the same committed state as the group listing gives the
required semantics without additional state or a per-partition scan.

Best,
Nicole

