Hi Federico,

Truncation-on-fetch was introduced in 2.7, but had edge cases, which were
fixed later. Commits like fcc7c2de391 and 8e211eb72f9 didn't go into 2.7.
There were also other fixes like KAFKA-12996 that came later than 2.8.0,
though that one is in 2.8.1. There may be others too. 3.0.x seems like a
safe option where we can expect truncation-on-fetch to be reliable.

Regards,

Rajini


